  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 159 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nSpotty showers have been popping up in association with a surface \nshortwave trough and the arrival of the seabreeze. These will \ncontinue to be isolated in nature and taper off this evening. Mid-\nlevel high pressure will dominate the period leading to warm and \nmostly rain free conditions outside of isolated seabreeze convection \neach day. This is thanks to some midlevel energy riding the \nperiphery of ridge as it builds from the east. Will continue to \nmonitor the need for some short- fused heat related products. We \ncould see heat indices up to 115 at times with dew points around the \nmid to upper 70s present through the next week. This translates to \nModerate to Major heat stress conditions though we could see some \nareas reach Extreme conditions by Wednesday. We strongly encourage \nthe practice of heat safety in these conditions. Take frequent \nbreaks and remember to stay hydrated, check those backseats, and \navoid long exposure in these temperatures. For more information be \nsure to check out weather.gov/heatsafety.",
